                "event": "Flash Flood Warning",
                "sender": "w-nws.webmaster@noaa.gov",
                "senderName": "NWS Flagstaff AZ",
                "headline": "Flash Flood Warning issued November 2 at 7:43AM MST until November 2 at 2:00PM MST by NWS Flagstaff AZ",
                "description": "FFWFGZ\n\nThe National Weather Service in Flagstaff has extended the\n\n* Flash Flood Warning for...\nCoconino County in north central Arizona...\nNavajo County in north central Arizona...\n\n* Until 200 PM MST Monday.\n\n* At 743 AM MST, a river gauge on the Little Colorado River at\nWinslow has rapidly risen to near Major flood stage due to upstream\nheavy rainfall. Additional rises to above Major flood stage are\nforecast shortly, with flooding impacts to Ames Acres and Bushman\nAcres in Winslow. Flash flooding is already occurring.\n\nHAZARD...Life threatening flash flooding. Heavy rain producing\nflash flooding.\n\nSOURCE...River gauge reported.\n\nIMPACT...Life threatening flash flooding of creeks and streams,\nnormally dry washes, urban areas, highways, streets and\nunderpasses.\n\n* For Little Colorado at Winslow:\nAt 7:00am MST the stage was 24.81 feet.\nFlood Stage is 19.0 feet.\nForecast: A crest of 46 feet is expected around 1:00am MST Monday.\nImpacts:\nAt 22.0 feet: Lowland flooding on right bank. Damage on left bank\nto Ames Acres and Bushman Acres in the event of levee failure.\nAt 25.0 feet: Levee is overtopped. Major flooding of portions of\nWinslow including Ames Acres and Bushman Acres.\n\nSome locations that will experience flash flooding include...\nWinslow, Leupp, Birdsprings, Sunrise, Bushman Acres and Homolovi\nRuins State Park.\n\nThis includes the following recreation areas and campgrounds...\nHomolovi State Park Campground.\n\nThis includes the following creeks, washes and rivers...\nLittle Colorado River.",
                "instruction": "Flooding of washes and creeks will occur, some dirt roads will become\nmuddy and impassable. Paved roads and underpasses could become\nflooded as well.\n\nBe aware of your surroundings and do not drive on flooded roads.\n\nLow water crossings will become dangerous in heavy rain. Do not\nattempt to cross flooded roads. Find an alternate route.",
                "response": "Avoid",
                "note": null,
                "parameters": {
                    "AWIPSidentifier": [
                        "FFWFGZ"
                    ],
                    "WMOidentifier": [
                        "WGUS55 KFGZ 021443"
                    ],
