                "senderName": "NWS Tampa Bay Ruskin FL",
                "headline": "Flash Flood Warning issued November 2 at 9:28AM EST until November 2 at 11:00AM EST by NWS Tampa Bay Ruskin FL",
                "description": "FFWTBW\n\nThe National Weather Service in Tampa Bay Ruskin has extended the\n\n* Flash Flood Warning for...\nEastern Hardee County in central Florida...\nNorthern DeSoto County in south central Florida...\nNorthwestern Highlands County in south central Florida...\n\n* Until 1100 AM EST.\n\n* At 928 AM EST, Emergency Management in DeSoto County reported\nthunderstorms producing heavy rain across the warned area. Water\nhas been reported entering structures. Between 5 and 9 inches of\nrain have fallen. Additional rainfall amounts of 2 to 3 inches are\npossible in the warned area. Flash flooding is already occurring.\n\nHAZARD...Life threatening flash flooding. Thunderstorms producing\nflash flooding.\n\nSOURCE...Emergency management reported.\n\nIMPACT...Life threatening flash flooding of creeks and streams,\nurban areas, highways, streets and underpasses.\n\n* Some locations that will experience flash flooding include...\nSebring, Avon Park, Arcadia, Wauchula, Southeast Arcadia, Sebring\nRegional Airport, Sweetwater, Zolfo Springs, Crewsville, Gardner,\nBrownville, Sebring Shores, Avon Park Executive Airport, Lake\nJosephine and Limestone.",
                "instruction": "Turn around, don't drown when encountering flooded roads. Most flood\ndeaths occur in vehicles.\n\nBe aware of your surroundings and do not drive on flooded roads.",
